    <statement><p>Racing cars driven by Chris and Kelly are side by side at the start of a race.  The table shows the velocities of each car (in miles per hour) during the first ten seconds of the race.</p>
<p><me>\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\hline
t \amp  v_C \amp  v_K \\ \hline
0       \amp  0               \amp  0               \\ \hline
1       \amp  20              \amp  22              \\ \hline
2       \amp  32              \amp  37              \\ \hline
3       \amp  46              \amp  52              \\ \hline
4       \amp  54              \amp  61              \\ \hline
5       \amp  62              \amp  71              \\ \hline
6       \amp  69              \amp  80              \\ \hline
7       \amp  75              \amp  86              \\ \hline
8       \amp  81              \amp  93              \\ \hline
9       \amp  86              \amp  98              \\ \hline
10      \amp  90              \amp  102             \\ \hline
\end{array}</me></p>
<p>Use the Midpoint Rule (with <m>n = 5</m>) to estimate how much farther (in feet) Kelly travels than Chris does during the first ten seconds.</p>
<p><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> feet</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>117.333333333333</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
